variables - in javascripts what is role of variables. can hold value which can be used in prgram or changed it later on.

Types of variables
1. var - var variableName
    scope - functions, variables- local/global, block - if, else, switch, try, catch
    function - if user declared var variable inside the function, scope of that variable would remained withint function only.
    Global(at class level) - if user declared var variable at global, can access across the class- inside function and out side function. 
    block - variable declared inside the block(if,else,switch,try,catch) scope would remain within that block only.

    var name = "Nitin"; // variable decalartion and initialization.
    var name = "sachin"; // re-declaration
    name = "abhishek"; // re-assigned

    re-declaration and re-allocation/re-assigned is allowed.

2. let - function + block + global
        let flag = true;
        let flag = false; // this is not allowed in let keyword | re-decalartion is not allow in let variable
        flag = false; re-allocation is allowed.

3. const - function + block + global
        1. re-declaration and re-allocation is not allowed in const.
        2. const is act as similar as final keyword in java




